From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 03:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: set the S6E8FC3X02 return packet size

The S6E8FC3X02 defaults to a one-byte DSI return packet.  Its display ID
is three bytes, so requesting the ID without first increasing the maximum
return packet size produces a valid one-byte short response and aborts
panel preparation.

Program the standard MIPI DSI maximum return packet size before reading
the ID.  The Nothing OS 4.1 MT6878 host performs the equivalent operation
automatically for every read; doing it in the panel driver keeps the
mainline host generic and uses the existing MIPI DSI API.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
index 19d2100..3ba6df1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
@@ -279,6 +279,12 @@ static int s6e8fc3x02_check_id(struct s6e8fc3x02 *ctx)
 	u8 id[ARRAY_SIZE(expected_id)];
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = mipi_dsi_set_maximum_return_packet_size(ctx->dsi, sizeof(id));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(&ctx->dsi->dev, ret,
+				     "failed to set maximum return packet size: %d\n",
+				     ret);
+
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_read(ctx->dsi, MIPI_DCS_GET_DISPLAY_ID,
 				id, sizeof(id));
 	if (ret < 0) {
